<BaseLayout title="About">
	<h1>About Us</h1>
    <h3>Welcome!</h3>
	<p>I'm Ashlar, and at Ashlar Tech Solutions, we put our faith into action. We believe that work is a form of service, 
            and we strive to use the talents given to us by our Lord to provide the best possible support for our clients.</p>

    <h3>What is an Ashlar?</h3>
    <p>In traditional stonecraft, an ashlar is a block that has been worked until it is perfectly 
            rectangular and smooth. While "rubble masonry" uses irregular, unworked stones, ashlar masonry is used for the world's 
            finest structures because the blocks fit together with incredible precision.</p>

    <h3>Our Mission</h3>
    <p>We see your business or organization as a grand structure. Each system—your network, your software, 
            your hardware—is a stone in that building. If the stones are rough and irregular, the foundation becomes unstable. 
            We specialize in smoothing those edges, ensuring every piece of your technology fits together perfectly to support your 
            mission.</p>
</BaseLayout>